+## TL;DR
+- `n8n`, `Activepieces`, and `Dify` are the strongest picks for small-business AI workflow automation and internal tools.
+- `AnythingLLM`, `Open WebUI`, `RAGFlow`, and `FastGPT` are the most practical choices for self-hosted AI chat, knowledge bases, and document Q&A.
+- `Docling`, `Langfuse`, and `LiteLLM` are strong infrastructure picks when a business needs better document processing, observability, or model routing.
+- `LibreChat`, `LobeHub`, and `Browser Use` are useful when teams need a polished interface around multiple models or browser-native task execution.
+- This topic is sparse if you search the exact phrase "AI tools for small businesses," so this list broadens honestly to open-source AI products that map well to real SMB workflows.
+
+## Why This List
+Most "best AI tools for small businesses" lists are affiliate-heavy SaaS comparisons. Small businesses often need lower cost, data control, self-hosting, and the ability to audit what their stack is doing. That makes GitHub-native AI software especially valuable in 2026: you can inspect the code, run it on your own infra, and avoid getting locked into proprietary pricing or roadmap decisions.
